<h1 style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:24px;font-weight:600;">Yes, you want a postcard</h1>
<p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#52525b;line-height:1.6;">
  You're subscribed to <a href="{{artistUrl}}" style="color:#18181b;"><strong>{{artistName}}</strong></a> for {{price}} a month{{#if oneMonth}}, for one month{{else}}, for {{termMonths}} months{{/if}}.
  Around the {{sendDay}}th of each month one of their postcards is printed and mailed to you — a photo they took and a short note on the back.
</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#52525b;line-height:1.6;">
  {{#if oneMonth}}One card, one payment, and it ends there.{{else}}You're billed each month, and after the {{termMonths}}th card it ends on its own — nothing to remember to cancel.{{/if}}
</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#52525b;line-height:1.6;">
  Nothing goes online. The card in your letterbox is the whole of it.
</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 0;">
  <a href="{{accountUrl}}" style="color:#18181b;">Your subscriptions, your address, and where each card is</a>
</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 0;color:#71717a;font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;">Cancel anytime from your account. You won't hurt anyone's feelings.</p>
